TI  - A Patient With Newly Diagnosed, Advanced EGFR-Mutated Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer.
PG  - 21-27
AB  - A 40-year-old woman presented with a productive cough and shortness of breath 
      that limited her regular activities. Her past medical history was relevant for 
      hypertension since 2016; it is well controlled and treated with enalapril 5 mg 
      twice daily. She also revealed a past wood smoke exposure of 2 hours per day for 
      10 years during her childhood. A chest computed tomography (CT) scan was 
      performed which showed a 30-mm lung nodule in the lower left lobe and mediastinal 
      and ipsilateral pleural thickening with moderate pleural effusion and several 
      bilateral lung metastases.
